%T A402441 2,1,6,11,1,3,14,31,1,5,2,7,11,5,5,23,3,1,2,3,1,5,6,31,2,1,2,11,1,3,5,
%U A402441 7,1,17,2,15,5,19,7,23,1,1,11,3,6,17,3,31,2
%N A402441 a(n) is the smallest k in [1,n] coprime to n such that -k is a quadratic residue modulo n.
%C A402441 a(n) is the minimal element of the coset of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing -1, where (Z/nZ)* is the multiplicative group of integers modulo n and (Z/nZ)*^2 is the subgroup of squares.
%C A402441 If n = p^e*s for p odd prime, e >= 2, and gcd(p,s) = 1, since squares modulo n and squares modulo p*s are the same, we have a(n) = a(p*s). Similarly, if n = 2^e*s for e >= 4 and odd s, then a(n) = a(8*s).
%C A402441 a(n) = 1 if and only if -1 is a quadratic residue modulo n (A008784).
%C A402441 Let N = 4*A002110(n+1) = A102476(n+2), then being a quadratic residue modulo N is equivalent to congruent to 1 modulo 8 and being a quadratic residue modulo every odd prime p <= prime(n+1), and so a(N) = A045535(n).
%H A402441 Jianing Song, <a href="/A402441/b402441.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A402441 a(n) = n - A402439(n) for n > 1.
%o A402441 (PARI) A402441(n) = for(d=1, n, if(gcd(d,n)==1 && issquare(Mod(-d,n)), return(d)))
%Y A402441 Cf. A008784, A402439, A045535.
%K A402441 nonn,new
%O A402441 1,3
%A A402441 _Jianing Song_, Nov 18 2026
